  "story_contract": {
    "opening_question": "Can a flood station judge rising street water with no power line and no cell tower?",
    "actor": "University of Texas at San Antonio researchers led by Chen Pan",
    "action": "Built a prototype flood station that charges itself from light and runs its AI model on a small chip.",
    "change": "A flood gauge that needs grid power and a network becomes a self-powered station that judges flood risk on its own chip and signals a hub by radio.",
    "affected_people": "Emergency responders and residents of street-level flood-prone blocks. No individual is named in any source.",
    "consequence": "A hub dashboard with predictive maps of how flooding could spread, for emergency responders, per the university.",
    "source_limit": "Disclosed illustration of the design the university describes. The accuracy is validation accuracy from initial assessments after training, the announcement reports no field result and names no installation.",
    "closing_answer": "The design says yes. The proof so far is validation accuracy, and the announcement names no installation.",
    "director_identity": "claude-sonnet-5-5 director, this session",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "scene_id": "s1",
        "role": "action",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c12"
        ],
        "advances": "A disclosed design detail with no yard around it: brown water climbs over the lowest optical lens at ankle height and the lens lights as it goes under. On the same ankle height the picture cuts to a San Antonio yard with no station in it, the water spreading past the orange ankle mark on a chain link post as the view pulls back. The water keeps rising to the rain boots on the porch step while the phone on the porch rail stays dark. The flash flood warning banner finally slides onto the phone, after the water is already in the yard."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s2",
        "role": "action",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c1",
          "c5",
          "c6",
          "c14"
        ],
        "advances": "The view cranes down from the antenna tip and reveals the whole prototype flood station at a curb, and a prototype tag pins. Low sun reaches the small dark solar panel, a glint crosses its cells and the battery bar fills cell by cell. A dashed line leaves the antenna toward a far cell tower and stops halfway, and a no cell tower needed tag pins."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s3",
        "role": "mechanism",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c2"
        ],
        "advances": "Four optical lenses at four different heights on the post catch the low light in turn. Flood water rises up the post past the second, third and fourth lenses, and each lens lights in turn as the waterline crosses it. The camera tilts down with the risen water and all four lit lenses under the surface flare one after another, from the highest to the lowest."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s4",
        "role": "mechanism",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c3",
          "c18"
        ],
        "advances": "Seen from the street through the housing window, readings run along the thin traces to the small chip. The chip lights the large amber risk lamp, the risk bar beside the board climbs from one low step to four and a judged on the station tag pins. Across the road a distant dark server building stays unlit, and a dashed line from the station stops short of it and never connects."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s5",
        "role": "mechanism",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c6"
        ],
        "advances": "From above, amber rings leave the station dot on the street map, the half-mile and five-mile labels appearing as each circle is reached. At street level the rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street. In open country rings roll out from the station in its inset to the hub's mast, the mast lamp and the hub window light as the leading ring arrives and the five-mile tag pins."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s6",
        "role": "consequence",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c7",
          "c16",
          "c17",
          "c20"
        ],
        "advances": "On the hub's screen, dots from several stations arrive and a tag names the second, larger model. Shaded flood paths spread out from the first dots along the creek and the low streets. At the desk the dashed higher-risk outlines settle on the screen, a responder's sleeved forearm comes to rest beside it and a for emergency responders tag pins."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s7",
        "role": "limit",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c4",
          "c18"
        ],
        "advances": "On the curb notice board the validation card is pinned up and an orange tape strip is pressed along its bar from end to end. The university's reported figure appears on the full bar and an initial assessments after training tag is pinned under the validation card. The blank field result card slides onto the board beside the validation card and a pushpin presses it home."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s8",
        "role": "limit",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c1",
          "c4",
          "c10"
        ],
        "advances": "On the same notice board the technician standing beside it brings a rubber stamp down onto the blank field result card, presses none reported and lifts it away. Wide on the empty curb after the flood, the paper street map pinned to the chain link fence settles, with no pin on it. The same technician slides one finger along the map's creek and up a street past a blank pin hole and lowers her arm. An announcement names no installation tag pins beside the map."
      },
      {
        "scene_id": "s9",
        "role": "answer",
        "claim_ids": [
          "c9",
          "c10"
        ],
        "advances": "Back in the flooded yard where the film began, the technician standing in the water opens the printed deployment plan out in one hand, the prototype's closed case held in the other. She looks up to the curb, an amber goal ring draws itself around a dashed unlit outline of the station at the curb and a field result tag reading none reported pins beside it. A deployment goal tag pins beside the ringed outline without covering it. She lowers the open plan and turns to the porch rail. The view follows her look in close to the still dark phone leaning on a small pot on the rail as rain drops strike its dark screen, then pulls back to the opening framing."
      }
